                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1de5cc86-40af-303e-972c-568b6a70556c",
                        "entry_id": "0d4a8232-6b0a-34cb-9a47-3df261028061",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take away humanity; to remove or deny human qualities, characteristics, or attributes; to impersonalize."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0781d29f-5a71-4ef7-ba4d-2626161f27b4",
                                "sense_id": "1de5cc86-40af-303e-972c-568b6a70556c",
                                "text": "In its consistently logical form Quietism makes communion between man and God an impossibility by annulling the distinction between them, ultimately reducing God to a vague and empty abstraction, and dehumanizing man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d6ac5fe-5998-492b-a79a-fffbb23963b4",
                                "sense_id": "1de5cc86-40af-303e-972c-568b6a70556c",
                                "text": "Yet we are dismayed by the failures and forces that dehumanize and defeat the finest dreams and plans of this generation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21b91371-c016-46d3-8c91-d339c149b0ec",
                                "sense_id": "1de5cc86-40af-303e-972c-568b6a70556c",
                                "text": "To what extent can we stop making the culture of the Other so dehumanized and Satanized as to make the Other fit to be genocidable?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ff12342-0d34-4a22-bd92-2d63df5b757b",
                                "sense_id": "1de5cc86-40af-303e-972c-568b6a70556c",
                                "text": "And, in this country, the traditional, ingrained way to dehumanize people, to make both their pain and their individuality irrelevant, is to rely on their race."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d046345-c837-4afe-809b-ef5d417ab44b",
                                "sense_id": "1de5cc86-40af-303e-972c-568b6a70556c",
                                "text": "A Melbourne woman says she feels “dehumanised” after being filmed without consent for a “random act of kindness” TikTok that went viral."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8742583-7be8-4f94-a232-a001ea138414",
                                "sense_id": "1de5cc86-40af-303e-972c-568b6a70556c",
                                "text": "From this sort of work, we learn to have a contempt for sadism, for anything that dehumanizes, and to have compassion for the everyday people who pay the price for the designs of proud and evil men."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
